00:33:53.410 --> 00:33:55.243
that Machine Learning
can provide a company.

00:33:57.610 --> 00:34:00.340
So at a high level,
this is what we

00:34:00.340 --> 00:34:03.060
have helped Discovery build
through the help of SDVI

00:34:03.060 --> 00:34:05.580
and Discovery.

00:34:05.580 --> 00:34:07.470
You can see on
the left, they are

00:34:07.470 --> 00:34:10.860
ingesting content from
multiple data sources.

00:34:10.860 --> 00:34:12.659
It gets ingested
into Google Cloud

00:34:12.659 --> 00:34:15.540
and stored on our
object storage.

00:34:15.540 --> 00:34:17.185
And then they can
run a transcode

00:34:17.185 --> 00:34:18.810
on that to create
the proxy file, which

00:34:18.810 --> 00:34:21.989
is what's going to be used
to run the ML APIs against.

00:34:21.989 --> 00:34:26.880
So you take that proxy file and
run it against each of the APIs

00:34:26.880 --> 00:34:29.070
and get all that JSON data back.

00:34:29.070 --> 00:34:31.572
And then you store it in
the SDVI Rally database.

00:34:31.572 --> 00:34:33.239
And that's where they
normalize the data

00:34:33.239 --> 00:34:35.790
and make sure it's in a format
that's ready to be consumed

00:34:35.790 --> 00:34:37.343
by an end user.

00:34:37.343 --> 00:34:38.760
And then on the
far right, you can

00:34:38.760 --> 00:34:42.449
see how somebody on-prem
or anywhere could

00:34:42.449 --> 00:34:45.659
go into Adobe Premiere, see
their task orders, their work

00:34:45.659 --> 00:34:48.989
orders, and actually start
to edit that content in Adobe

00:34:48.989 --> 00:34:53.596
Premiere, pulling that ML
metadata out of the Cloud.

00:34:53.596 --> 00:34:55.679
So I'm going to show you
a video of how this looks

00:34:55.679 --> 00:34:58.220
in SDVI's Rally Access panel.

00:34:58.220 --> 00:35:00.280
So you select your task order.

00:35:00.280 --> 00:35:02.070
You can go in and
select the labels

00:35:02.070 --> 00:35:04.650
with the time-based
metadata showing up.

00:35:04.650 --> 00:35:07.380
On the left, you'll see
that there's actually

00:35:07.380 --> 00:35:12.090
time-based metadata for
each label with ins and outs

00:35:12.090 --> 00:35:14.380
for that particular label.

00:35:14.380 --> 00:35:16.050
So you see they can
select one, and it

00:35:16.050 --> 00:35:19.710
shows right on the editing
panel where that video is.

00:35:19.710 --> 00:35:23.220
So if you need to search
for some explicit content,

00:35:23.220 --> 00:35:26.610
for example, that would take you
right to that point in video.

00:35:26.610 --> 00:35:28.200
So you're not
spending time looking

00:35:28.200 --> 00:35:31.020
through that entire video trying
to find specific things that

00:35:31.020 --> 00:35:32.640
need to be QCed.

00:35:32.640 --> 00:35:35.160
So you can also see
in the middle there,

00:35:35.160 --> 00:35:38.020
they have the time codes
right in the sequence.

00:35:38.020 --> 00:35:39.960
So you can go in and
see exactly as you're

00:35:39.960 --> 00:35:42.120
scanning through that
file what the labels are

00:35:42.120 --> 00:35:44.540
during that sequence.

00:35:44.540 --> 00:35:48.460
So this is what Discovery
is utilizing today,

00:35:48.460 --> 00:35:51.160
with the help of SDVI and our
Machine Learning technology.

00:35:54.032 --> 00:35:55.740
Now, I want to talk
to you a little bit--

00:35:55.740 --> 00:35:58.760
how can you get started
doing this yourself?

00:35:58.760 --> 00:36:00.290
And there's really three ways.

00:36:00.290 --> 00:36:02.285
One is talk to
your account team,

00:36:02.285 --> 00:36:05.625
you know, somebody like me,
a Google Customer Engineer.

00:36:05.625 --> 00:36:07.250
And we can help guide
you through this,

00:36:07.250 --> 00:36:09.680
give you demos, get you in
touch with partners on how

00:36:09.680 --> 00:36:11.270
to build this yourselves.

00:36:11.270 --> 00:36:14.010
You can talk to the
partners themselves.

00:36:14.010 --> 00:36:17.300
They can show you what their
technology can do and help you.

00:36:17.300 --> 00:36:19.550
And then you can engage with
our Professional Services

00:36:19.550 --> 00:36:20.092
organization.

00:36:20.092 --> 00:36:21.717
And they're the ones
that will actually

00:36:21.717 --> 00:36:23.660
come in and help build
this with you, actually

00:36:23.660 --> 00:36:24.952
deploy it in your environments.

00:36:24.952 --> 00:36:27.190
[MUSIC PLAYING]

